 [3,4,5,8], SSE = 2, SST = 20, R² = 0.90.</p></section>",
  "questions": [
    {
      "stem": "What is R-squared (R²) in regression, and how does it measure model fit compared with predicting the mean of the actual target values?",
      "tag": "Beginner · R² definition",
      "options": [
        "R-squared compares average absolute prediction error with the average target value. A model scores higher when its typical error is small compared with the mean, regardless of how much the true values vary.",
        "R-squared is the share of numerical predictions that fall within a chosen error tolerance. It counts accepted test records instead of comparing squared model mistakes with a mean-value baseline.",
        "R-squared compares a model's squared prediction mistakes with errors from always predicting the evaluated targets' mean: R² = 1 − SSE/SST. Higher values reflect improvement over that baseline.",
        "R-squared compares squared prediction errors against the model's own training errors. It measures how training improved the predictions rather than how the model performs against a constant-value mean baseline."
      ],
      "answer": "c",
      "explanation": "<strong>Explanation:</strong> R-squared (R²), or the coefficient of determination, compares squared prediction errors against a baseline that predicts the mean of the evaluated target values. Its formula is 1 − SSE/SST, where SSE is the model's sum of squared errors and SST is the total squared deviation from the target mean. For a café's daily sales forecast, R² 0.90 means 90% less squared error than that mean baseline on the evaluated records—not 90% exactly correct predictions.",
      "figure": "<section class=\"rsq-figure\"><span class=\"rsq-kicker\">QUESTION 01 · VISUAL LESSON</span><div class=\"rsq-art\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 1000 440\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"r2title1 r2desc1\"><title id=\"r2title1\">How much better than guessing the mean?</title><desc id=\"r2desc1\">Plot of four actual and predicted values with the SSE and SST that define R-squared.</desc><rect width=\"1000\" height=\"440\" fill=\"#f8fcfd\"/><text x=\"38\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#278978\" font-weight=\"850\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">01 · R-SQUARED</text><text x=\"38\" y=\"78\" font-size=\"25\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#2d566b\" font-weight=\"850\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">How much better than guessing the mean?</text><rect x=\"31\" y=\"115\" width=\"585\" height=\"256\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#d8e5ea\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"55\" y=\"149\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#4f7e94\" font-weight=\"850\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">OBSERVED vs PREDICTED</text><line x1=\"81\" y1=\"346\" x2=\"573\" y2=\"346\" stroke=\"#8ba9b8\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"151\" y1=\"296\" x2=\"151\" y2=\"271\" stroke=\"#df9e70\" stroke-width=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"151\" cy=\"296\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#3aa58c\"/><circle cx=\"151\" cy=\"271\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#df9e70\"/><text x=\"151\" y=\"373\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#5a7e90\" font-weight=\"600\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Record 1</text><line x1=\"260\" y1=\"246\" x2=\"260\" y2=\"246\" stroke=\"#df9e70\" stroke-width=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"260\" cy=\"246\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#3aa58c\"/><circle cx=\"260\" cy=\"246\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#df9e70\"/><text x=\"260\" y=\"373\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#5a7e90\" font-weight=\"600\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Record 2</text><line x1=\"369\" y1=\"196\" x2=\"369\" y2=\"221\" stroke=\"#df9e70\" stroke-width=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"369\" cy=\"196\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#3aa58c\"/><circle cx=\"369\" cy=\"221\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#df9e70\"/><text x=\"369\" y=\"373\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#5a7e90\" font-weight=\"600\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Record 3</text><line x1=\"478\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"478\" y2=\"146\" stroke=\"#df9e70\" stroke-width=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"478\" cy=\"146\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#3aa58c\"/><circle cx=\"478\" cy=\"146\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#df9e70\"/><text x=\"478\" y=\"373\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#5a7e90\" font-weight=\"600\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Record 4</text><text x=\"57\" y=\"402\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#507b88\" font-weight=\"680\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Teal = actual   Orange = predicted</text><rect x=\"634\" y=\"115\" width=\"337\" height=\"256\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#d8e5ea\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"653\" y=\"155\" font-size=\"17\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#548297\" font-weight=\"850\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">THE MEAN BASELINE</text><text x=\"658\" y=\"211\" font-size=\"28\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#3d91ad\" font-weight=\"830\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">SSE = 2</text><text x=\"658\" y=\"259\" font-size=\"28\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#3d91ad\" font-weight=\"830\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">SST = 20</text><text x=\"658\" y=\"332\" font-size=\"24\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#218d7c\" font-weight=\"860\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">R² = 1 − 2/20 = 0.90</text></svg></div><p class=\"rsq-note\">The baseline is the mean of the target values in the evaluated set.</p></section>"
