    {
      "stem": "What do R-squared values of 1, 0, and below 0 mean, and why can an evaluated regression model receive a negative score?",
      "tag": "Beginner · Negative R²",
      "options": [
        "An R² of 1 means every result rounds correctly, 0 means target values have no variation, and negative values mean the actual targets contain negative numbers. Nonnegative targets therefore cannot produce negative R².",
        "An R² of 1 means perfect correlation, 0 means no correlation, and values below zero show inverse correlation. Just like a Pearson correlation coefficient, R-squared must stay between −1 and 1.",
        "An R² of 1 means zero training loss, 0 means half the predictions are correct, and negative results show the model's intercept is negative. Evaluation on unseen records cannot produce negative values.",
        "An R² of 1 indicates perfect predictions, 0 matches the evaluated set's mean baseline, and a negative score means more squared error than that baseline. Negative R² is possible, particularly on unseen data."
      ],
      "answer": "d",
      "explanation": "<strong>Explanation:</strong> An R² of 1 means perfect predictions; 0 matches the squared error of the evaluation target's mean baseline. A negative value means the model's squared error exceeds that baseline. It can even fall below −1. For a taxi-distance forecast with actual values [2,4,6,8], predicting 7 for all four journeys gives SSE = 36 and SST = 20, so R² = −0.80. Negative R² is a meaningful warning, not necessarily a calculation mistake.",
      "figure": "<section class=\"rsq-figure\"><span class=\"rsq-kicker\">QUESTION 03 · VISUAL LESSON</span><div class=\"rsq-art\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 1000 440\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"r2title3 r2desc3\"><title id=\"r2title3\">Why R² can be perfect, zero, or negative</title><desc id=\"r2desc3\">Perfect predictions R-squared one, mean-only prediction R-squared zero, predictions of 7 for every example yield R-squared minus 0.8.</desc><rect width=\"1000\" height=\"440\" fill=\"#f8fcfd\"/><text x=\"38\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#278978\" font-weight=\"850\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">03 · R-SQUARED</text><text x=\"38\" y=\"78\" font-size=\"25\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#2d566b\" font-weight=\"850\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Why R² can be perfect, zero, or negative</text><rect x=\"31\" y=\"118\" width=\"306\" height=\"261\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#eaf8f1\" stroke=\"#d8e5ea\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"49\" y=\"150\" font-size=\"17\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#4e788c\" font-weight=\"840\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">PERFECT</text><line x1=\"66\" y1=\"306\" x2=\"311\" y2=\"306\" stroke=\"#8ba9b8\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"84\" cy=\"303\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#3aa58c\"/><circle cx=\"151\" cy=\"257\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#3aa58c\"/><circle cx=\"218\" cy=\"211\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#3aa58c\"/><circle cx=\"285\" cy=\"165\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#3aa58c\"/><path d=\"M84 303 L151 257 L218 211 L285 165\" stroke=\"#a2c4c5\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M84 303 L151 257 L218 211 L285 165\" stroke=\"#3aa58c\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"184\" y=\"352\" font-size=\"25\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#3aa58c\" font-weight=\"850\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">R² = 1.00</text><rect x=\"348\" y=\"118\" width=\"306\" height=\"261\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#ecf8fd\" stroke=\"#d8e5ea\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"366\" y=\"150\" font-size=\"17\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#4e788c\" font-weight=\"840\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">MEAN BASELINE</text><line x1=\"383\" y1=\"306\" x2=\"628\" y2=\"306\" stroke=\"#8ba9b8\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"401\" cy=\"234\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#3d91ad\"/><circle cx=\"468\" cy=\"234\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#3d91ad\"/><circle cx=\"535\" cy=\"234\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#3d91ad\"/><circle cx=\"602\" cy=\"234\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#3d91ad\"/><path d=\"M401 303 L468 257 L535 211 L602 165\" stroke=\"#a2c4c5\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M401 234 L468 234 L535 234 L602 234\" stroke=\"#3d91ad\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"501\" y=\"352\" font-size=\"25\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#3d91ad\" font-weight=\"850\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">R² = 0.00</text><rect x=\"665\" y=\"118\" width=\"306\" height=\"261\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#fff3e9\" stroke=\"#d8e5ea\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"683\" y=\"150\" font-size=\"17\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#4e788c\" font-weight=\"840\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">WORSE THAN MEAN</text><line x1=\"700\" y1=\"306\" x2=\"945\" y2=\"306\" stroke=\"#8ba9b8\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"718\" cy=\"188\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#df9e70\"/><circle cx=\"785\" cy=\"188\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#df9e70\"/><circle cx=\"852\" cy=\"188\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#df9e70\"/><circle cx=\"919\" cy=\"188\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#df9e70\"/><path d=\"M718 303 L785 257 L852 211 L919 165\" stroke=\"#a2c4c5\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M718 188 L785 188 L852 188 L919 188\" stroke=\"#df9e70\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"818\" y=\"352\" font-size=\"25\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#df9e70\" font-weight=\"850\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">R² = −0.80</text></svg></div><p class=\"rsq-note\">Unlike correlation, R² is not confined to the interval from −1 to 1.</p></section>"
