    {
      "stem": "How does R-squared differ from Mean Squared Error (MSE), and why can two datasets have the same MSE but different R-squared scores?",
      "tag": "Medium · MSE and target spread",
      "options": [
        "R-squared and MSE both measure squared prediction errors in squared target units, but R-squared divides by the number of records twice. Equal MSE scores therefore always imply identical R-squared values.",
        "MSE averages squared mistakes in the target's squared units. R-squared compares the total squared error with variation in the evaluated true values, so identical MSE can produce different R² scores.",
        "MSE measures the average squared mistake, while R-squared counts the fraction of perfectly predicted numerical values. Equal MSE can yield different R² only when the number of test cases differs.",
        "R-squared is obtained by dividing the square root of MSE by the target variance. Its result is unitless, so comparing its scores across different datasets never requires checking target variability."
      ],
      "answer": "b",
      "explanation": "<strong>Explanation:</strong> MSE averages squared prediction errors, giving an answer in squared target units. R² compares those squared errors with variation in the true targets, so it is unitless but still dataset-dependent. With actual values [0,2] and predictions [1,3], MSE = 1 and R² = 0. With actual values [0,10] and predictions [1,11], MSE remains 1 but R² rises to 0.96. A temperature forecast may therefore have identical MSE across two regions yet different R² because their temperatures vary differently.",
      "figure": "<section class=\"rsq-figure\"><span class=\"rsq-kicker\">QUESTION 04 · VISUAL LESSON</span><div class=\"rsq-art\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 1000 440\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"r2title4 r2desc4\"><title id=\"r2title4\">Identical MSE, dramatically different R²</title><desc id=\"r2desc4\">Two toy datasets have MSE one but target variances differ: actual 0,2 produces R-squared zero while actual 0,10 produces 0.96.</desc><rect width=\"1000\" height=\"440\" fill=\"#f8fcfd\"/><text x=\"38\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#278978\" font-weight=\"850\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">04 · R-SQUARED</text><text x=\"38\" y=\"78\" font-size=\"25\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#2d566b\" font-weight=\"850\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Identical MSE, dramatically different R²</text><rect x=\"29\" y=\"116\" width=\"453\" height=\"258\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#edf7fb\" stroke=\"#d8e5ea\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"51\" y=\"153\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#3d91ad\" font-weight=\"840\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">SMALL TARGET SPREAD</text><text x=\"53\" y=\"194\" font-size=\"19\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#345a70\" font-weight=\"700\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Actual: [0, 2]</text><text x=\"53\" y=\"226\" font-size=\"19\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#345a70\" font-weight=\"700\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Predicted: [1, 3]</text><line x1=\"77\" y1=\"258\" x2=\"445\" y2=\"258\" stroke=\"#8ba9b8\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"82\" cy=\"258\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#3aa58c\"/><circle cx=\"112.9090909090909\" cy=\"258\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#df9e70\"/><circle cx=\"143.8181818181818\" cy=\"258\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#3aa58c\"/><circle cx=\"174.72727272727272\" cy=\"258\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#df9e70\"/><text x=\"52\" y=\"312\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#5f7e8e\" font-weight=\"690\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">MSE = 1  ·  SST = 2</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"354\" font-size=\"27\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#3d91ad\" font-weight=\"870\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">R² = 0.00</text><rect x=\"519\" y=\"116\" width=\"453\" height=\"258\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#edf9f1\" stroke=\"#d8e5ea\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"541\" y=\"153\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#3aa58c\" font-weight=\"840\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">LARGE TARGET SPREAD</text><text x=\"543\" y=\"194\" font-size=\"19\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#345a70\" font-weight=\"700\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Actual: [0, 10]</text><text x=\"543\" y=\"226\" font-size=\"19\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#345a70\" font-weight=\"700\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Predicted: [1, 11]</text><line x1=\"567\" y1=\"258\" x2=\"935\" y2=\"258\" stroke=\"#8ba9b8\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"572\" cy=\"258\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#3aa58c\"/><circle cx=\"602.9090909090909\" cy=\"258\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#df9e70\"/><circle cx=\"881.090909090909\" cy=\"258\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#3aa58c\"/><circle cx=\"912\" cy=\"258\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#df9e70\"/><text x=\"542\" y=\"312\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#5f7e8e\" font-weight=\"690\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">MSE = 1  ·  SST = 50</text><text x=\"542\" y=\"354\" font-size=\"27\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#3aa58c\" font-weight=\"870\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">R² = 0.96</text></svg></div><p class=\"rsq-note\">A unitless R² still depends on which target distribution you evaluate.</p></section>"
    },
    {
      "stem": "How can R-squared be calculated using Scikit-learn on held-out regression data, and why must preprocessing and model selection avoid test-set leakage?",
      "tag": "Medium · Python held-out scoring",
      "options": [
        "Split data, but fit the feature scaler on both training and test records before model training. Computing r2_score afterward still gives an unbiased holdout result because scaling cannot influence model selection.",
        "Fit a regression model on all available target labels, calculate r2_score on those same fitted records, and treat the result as a final benchmark because the mean baseline eliminates evaluation leakage.",
        "Split data before fitting, train preprocessing and regression using only training records, then call r2_score(y_test, predictions) on untouched test cases. Check it with a manual SSE/SST calculation.",
        "Split the data, select features using final test labels, then train a regression model on the training partition. Test results remain unbiased because the holdout labels were used only for feature selection."
      ],
      "answer": "c",
      "explanation": "<strong>Explanation:</strong> Divide the dataset before fitting transformations. Train the scaler and regressor using only training cases, predict the held-out records, and calculate r2_score(y_test, predictions). The mean of test labels appears in the metric's denominator only after predictions have been made; this is not training leakage. The example Python script scores approximately 0.9873 on 60 unseen synthetic records. In public-bus arrival forecasting, tuning features using final test outcomes would produce overly optimistic results.",
      "figure": "<section class=\"rsq-figure\"><span class=\"rsq-kicker\">QUESTION 05 · VISUAL LESSON</span><div class=\"rsq-art\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 1000 440\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"r2title5 r2desc5\"><title id=\"r2title5\">Train only on past samples; score unseen predictions</title><desc id=\"r2desc5\">Scikit-learn pipeline trained on 180 synthetic records and scored on 60 held-out regression examples yields R-squared about 0.9873.</desc><rect width=\"1000\" height=\"440\" fill=\"#f8fcfd\"/><text x=\"38\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#278978\" font-weight=\"850\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">05 · R-SQUARED</text><text x=\"38\" y=\"78\" font-size=\"25\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#2d566b\" font-weight=\"850\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Train only on past samples; score unseen predictions</text><rect x=\"29\" y=\"111\" width=\"938\" height=\"265\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#d8e5ea\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><rect x=\"57\" y=\"163\" width=\"194\" height=\"121\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#e9f7fc\" stroke=\"#d8e5ea\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"154\" y=\"204\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#3d91ad\" font-weight=\"840\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">TRAIN DATA</text><text x=\"154\" y=\"248\" font-size=\"17\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#517587\" font-weight=\"670\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">180 examples</text><rect x=\"328\" y=\"163\" width=\"252\" height=\"121\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#f1f2fc\" stroke=\"#d8e5ea\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"454\" y=\"204\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#65739e\" font-weight=\"840\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">FIT PIPELINE</text><text x=\"454\" y=\"248\" font-size=\"17\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#517587\" font-weight=\"670\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Scaler + Ridge</text><rect x=\"664\" y=\"163\" width=\"274\" height=\"121\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#eaf8ee\" stroke=\"#d8e5ea\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"801\" y=\"204\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#3aa58c\" font-weight=\"840\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">TEST R²</text><text x=\"801\" y=\"248\" font-size=\"17\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#517587\" font-weight=\"670\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">60 cases · 0.9873</text><path d=\"M257 224 H316 M306 214 L316 224 L306 234\" stroke=\"#6c9ca8\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M589 224 H653 M643 214 L653 224 L643 234\" stroke=\"#6c9ca8\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"59\" y=\"339\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#3d6a7b\" font-weight=\"730\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">The test-set mean is used only after prediction, to calculate the metric.</text></svg></div><div class=\"rsq-code\"><div class=\"rsq-code-head\">Python · Scikit-learn · 14 executable lines</div><pre style=\"background:#1e1e1e;color:#eff9ff;overflow-x:auto;white-space:pre\"><code style=\"background:transparent!important;color:#eff9ff!important;border:0!important;padding:0!important;display:block;font:inherit;white-space:pre\">from sklearn.datasets import make_regression\nfrom sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\nfrom sklearn.pipeline import make_pipeline\nfrom sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\nfrom sklearn.linear_model import Ridge\nfrom sklearn.metrics import r2_score\nimport numpy as np\nX,y = make_regression(n_samples=240,n_features=4,noise=12,random_state=17)\nXtr,Xte,ytr,yte = train_test_split(X,y,test_size=.25,random_state=42)\nmodel = make_pipeline(StandardScaler(),Ridge(alpha=1.0))\nmodel.fit(Xtr,ytr)\npred = model.predict(Xte)\nprint(round(r2_score(yte,pred),4))\nprint(round(1-np.sum((yte-pred)**2)/np.sum((yte-yte.mean())**2),4))</code></pre></div><p class=\"rsq-note\">Q5 contains a runnable 14-line Scikit-learn example and its manual SSE/SST check.</p></section>"
    },
    {
      "stem": "Why can adding predictors raise training R-squared in ordinary least-squares regression, and how does adjusted R-squared account for model complexity?",
      "tag": "Advanced · Adjusted R²",
      "options": [
        "In ordinary least squares with an intercept, adding predictors cannot lower training R² because old coefficients remain possible. Adjusted R² uses sample size and predictor count to penalize extra complexity, sometimes decreasing.",
        "In ordinary least squares with an intercept, every added predictor lowers training R² unless it is statistically significant. Adjusted R² removes this effect, so its score always increases as predictors accumulate.",
        "Training R² is unchanged by adding predictors because it depends solely on target variance. Adjusted R² instead multiplies the score by the number of features, consistently rewarding more complex models.",
        "Training R² may increase when predictors are added, but adjusted R² penalizes complexity by squaring every model error again. Its value is independent of sample size and number of observations."
      ],
      "answer": "a",
      "explanation": "<strong>Explanation:</strong> With ordinary least-squares regression and an intercept, adding predictors cannot reduce training R² because the model can assign zero coefficients to new features. Adjusted R² accounts for sample size and predictor count using 1 − (1−R²)(n−1)/(n−p−1). For 30 cases and training R² 0.80, three predictors give adjusted R² about 0.777; ten give about 0.695. In an apartment-price model, irrelevant amenities can boost training fit without helping future predictions, so an independent test remains essential.",
      "figure": "<section class=\"rsq-figure\"><span class=\"rsq-kicker\">QUESTION 06 · VISUAL LESSON</span><div class=\"rsq-art\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 1000 440\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"r2title6 r2desc6\"><title id=\"r2title6\">Extra features are not free</title><desc id=\"r2desc6\">For 30 examples and training R-squared 0.8, adjusted R-squared with 3 predictors is about 0.777 and with 10 predictors about 0.695.</desc><rect width=\"1000\" height=\"440\" fill=\"#f8fcfd\"/><text x=\"38\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#278978\" font-weight=\"850\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">06 · R-SQUARED</text><text x=\"38\" y=\"78\" font-size=\"25\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#2d566b\" font-weight=\"850\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Extra features are not free</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"112\" width=\"938\" height=\"267\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#d8e5ea\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"53\" y=\"150\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#4e7a8e\" font-weight=\"830\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">SAME TRAINING R² 0.80 · 30 EXAMPLES · ORDINARY LEAST SQUARES</text><text x=\"69\" y=\"198\" font-size=\"21\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#3f6c7c\" font-weight=\"810\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">3 predictors</text><rect x=\"69\" y=\"224\" width=\"349\" height=\"31\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#edf2f5\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><rect x=\"69\" y=\"224\" width=\"271.1461538461538\" height=\"31\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#3aa58c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"69\" y=\"295\" font-size=\"22\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#3aa58c\" font-weight=\"840\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Adjusted R² = 0.777</text><text x=\"526\" y=\"198\" font-size=\"21\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#3f6c7c\" font-weight=\"810\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">10 predictors</text><rect x=\"526\" y=\"224\" width=\"349\" height=\"31\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#edf2f5\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><rect x=\"526\" y=\"224\" width=\"242.4631578947368\" height=\"31\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#df9e70\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"526\" y=\"295\" font-size=\"22\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#df9e70\" font-weight=\"840\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Adjusted R² = 0.695</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"354\" font-size=\"20\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#3b6577\" font-weight=\"820\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Adjusted R² = 1 − (1 − R²) × (n − 1) / (n − p − 1)</text></svg></div><p class=\"rsq-note\">Adjusted R² is a training-fit complexity correction, not a substitute for held-out evaluation.</p></section>"
    },
    {
      "stem": "How should R-squared be evaluated and reported across time, subgroups, changing target variance, and multiple outputs, including the constant-target edge case?",
      "tag": "Advanced · Production benchmarking",
      "options": [
        "Report only global training R² since it is dimensionless and directly comparable across arbitrary datasets. Changes in the target's variation, group composition, or constant labels cannot alter its interpretation or usefulness.",
        "Use random splits for every forecasting task and average subgroup R² without checking target distributions. Constant targets always produce a defined R² of zero, even when every prediction is exactly correct.",
        "Choose model features with the final holdout, then reuse that same score for reporting. Combine multiple predicted outputs by adding their target values before computing one universal R².",
        "Use leakage-free time- or group-aware holdouts, report target variation and subgroup R², and monitor drift. State multioutput aggregation explicitly; ordinary R² is undefined when every evaluated target is constant."
      ],
      "answer": "d",
      "explanation": "<strong>Explanation:</strong> R² depends on target variation, so report evaluation-set composition, uncertainty when useful, subgroup results, and error metrics alongside it. Preserve chronology for forecasting and group boundaries for repeated records. For multiple targets, state the averaging method. If evaluated targets are constant, the ordinary R² denominator is zero and the score is undefined; Scikit-learn usually substitutes finite values by default. A regional energy forecast might score 0.88 in one region but 0.31 in another, hiding a deployment weakness behind the global average.",
      "figure": "<section class=\"rsq-figure\"><span class=\"rsq-kicker\">QUESTION 07 · VISUAL LESSON</span><div class=\"rsq-art\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 1000 440\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"r2title7 r2desc7\"><title id=\"r2title7\">Time, subgroup variation, and constant targets</title><desc id=\"r2desc7\">Chronological train validation test illustration plus group R-squared comparisons. Constant evaluation targets make normal R-squared undefined.</desc><rect width=\"1000\" height=\"440\" fill=\"#f8fcfd\"/><text x=\"38\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#278978\" font-weight=\"850\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">07 · R-SQUARED</text><text x=\"38\" y=\"78\" font-size=\"25\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#2d566b\" font-weight=\"850\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Time, subgroup variation, and constant targets</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"112\" width=\"940\" height=\"262\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#d8e5ea\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"55\" y=\"152\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#537e92\" font-weight=\"840\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">TIME-BASED HOLDOUT: FUTURE RECORDS MUST STAY UNSEEN</text><rect x=\"55\" y=\"167\" width=\"213\" height=\"82\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#eaf7fd\" stroke=\"#d8e5ea\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"161.5\" y=\"218\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#3d91ad\" font-weight=\"850\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">2024 · FIT</text><rect x=\"281\" y=\"167\" width=\"215\" height=\"82\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#f1f3fd\" stroke=\"#d8e5ea\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"388.5\" y=\"218\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6d7da1\" font-weight=\"850\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">2025 · TUNE</text><rect x=\"509\" y=\"167\" width=\"438\" height=\"82\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#e7f9f0\" stroke=\"#d8e5ea\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"728\" y=\"218\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#3aa58c\" font-weight=\"850\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">2026 · TEST · untouched</text><text x=\"57\" y=\"289\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#527e90\" font-weight=\"830\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">SUBGROUP R² FROM HELD-OUT EVALUATION</text><text x=\"57\" y=\"341\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#4e7485\" font-weight=\"800\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Region A</text><rect x=\"173\" y=\"323\" width=\"186\" height=\"23\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#e7eff2\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><rect x=\"173\" y=\"323\" width=\"163.68\" height=\"23\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#3aa58c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"373\" y=\"342\" font-size=\"19\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#3aa58c\" font-weight=\"850\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">0.88</text><text x=\"502\" y=\"341\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#4e7485\" font-weight=\"800\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">Region B</text><rect x=\"618\" y=\"323\" width=\"186\" height=\"23\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#e7eff2\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><rect x=\"618\" y=\"323\" width=\"57.66\" height=\"23\" rx=\"12\" fill=\"#df9e70\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"818\" y=\"342\" font-size=\"19\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#df9e70\" font-weight=\"850\" font-family=\"system-ui,Arial,sans-serif\">0.31</text></svg></div><p class=\"rsq-note\">For constant true labels, Scikit-learn r2_score defaults to force_finite=True.</p></section>"
    }
